Third-party code in this repository
===================================

This project is distributed under the MIT license (see LICENSE). Two groups of
files come from elsewhere and keep their own terms.

1. Derived from phacility/xhprof (Apache License 2.0)
----------------------------------------------------

The report rendering and run-storage layer is derived from phacility/xhprof:

  src/Core/XhprofLib/**            (display, lib and run-store classes)
  src/html/js/xhprof_report.js     (carries the upstream Facebook/Apache header)
  src/html/css/**, src/html/images/**

phacility/xhprof is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://github.com/phacility/xhprof — verified 2026-09-25). Those files are
used and modified under that license; the modifications are the multi-framework
adapters, the i18n layer, and the fixes recorded in this repository's history.

2. Redistributed third-party front-end libraries
------------------------------------------------

src/html/ ships unmodified copies of libraries that the report page loads:

  jquery/jquery-3.0.0.min.js          jQuery (jQuery Foundation)
  js/bootstrap.min.js, css/bootstrap.css   Bootstrap 3 (MIT — header present)
  js/jquery.dataTables.min.js, js/dataTables.bootstrap.js, css/dataTables.bootstrap.css
                                       DataTables 1.10.15 (DataTables)
  js/bootstrap-table.js, js/bootstrap-table-zh-CN.js   bootstrap-table
  js/jquery.autocomplete.js, js/jquery.tooltip.js, jquery/jquery-1.2.6.js
                                       jQuery plugins of the same vintage

Their own license terms apply (jQuery, Bootstrap, DataTables and bootstrap-table
are all MIT-licensed upstream); where the upstream file shipped a license header
it is kept verbatim in the file.

Two of these libraries are currently **not** loaded by the report page
(`xhprof_include_js_css()` loads five scripts): `bootstrap-table.js` (and its
Chinese locale file) and the jQuery 1.2.6 / autocomplete / tooltip trio, the
last of which predates jQuery 3 and is kept only because the parent/child
tooltip code was ported from upstream. They are listed here for completeness,
not because they are active.
